  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "dxf_blocks_read",
    "file": "libredwg/src/in_dxf.c",
    "description": "In dxf_blocks_read, a heap string is created with `dxfname = strdup(pair->value.s)` and passed into `new_object(name, dxfname, ...)`, which stores it in the object for later cleanup. On the error path when `new_object` returns NULL, the function immediately calls `free(dxfname)` before returning. The partially constructed object still retains that same pointer, so later `dwg_free` -> `free_preR13_object` frees `obj->dxfname` again, causing a double-free.",
    "conditions": "Trigger requires DXF input parsed by `dwg_read_dxf` (llvmfuzz default non-DWG/non-JSON path) that reaches `dxf_blocks_read` and causes `new_object(...)` to fail/return NULL after `dxfname` was strdup'ed and attached to object state. The function frees `dxfname` on this failure path but does not clear/rollback object ownership, and subsequent global cleanup (`dwg_free`) frees object `dxfname` again."
  },
